			<view isee:template_view="template:8" background="white" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="85" type="interface">
				<style/>
				<text_box font_weight="bold" font_color="white" font_size="36pt" appearance="transparent" x="33.5294" y="16.4706" width="561.176" height="58">HIV Incidence and Prevalence </text_box>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:2" background="white" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="115" type="interface">
				<style>
					<isee:stacked_container item_spacing="0" corner_radius="4" selected_item_color="black" selected_item_background="white" item_background="#DDDDDD" transparent_bg="false"/>
				</style>
				<text_box border_color="blue" border_width="2" x="21.7826" y="79.587" width="628.25" height="573">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;.AppleSystemUIFont&apos;; font-size:13pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt;&quot;&gt;In system dynamics modeling, four key types of validity are used to assess whether a model is credible, useful, and appropriate for decision-making. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;Here are four focused questions for each type of validity that can help assess whether our current SD model of PrEP reach appears useful for next steps in our project:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt; color:#000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;1. Structural Validity &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt;&quot;&gt;Does the model include all key drivers and realistically represent how they interact through feedback loops to influence PrEP uptake over time? &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;2. Behavioral Validity &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt;&quot;&gt;Do the model’s trends match real-world data, and are projected outcomes plausible? &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;3. Construct Validity &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt;&quot;&gt;Does the model meaningfully capture the core problem of limited PrEP reach and inform actionable intervention strategies? &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;4. Data Validity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:14pt;&quot;&gt;Are the data sources used for calibration and parameter estimation sufficiently accurate, recent, and representative of plausible model outputs? &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text_box>
				<text_box font_weight="bold" text_align="center" vertical_text_align="center" font_size="24pt" appearance="transparent" x="11.4107" y="8.42857" width="625.286" height="50">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;.AppleSystemUIFont&apos;; font-size:13pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:24pt; font-weight:700; color:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;Systems Dynamics Validity Assessment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text_box>
				<graphics_frame fill="none" x="63.4783" y="173.043" width="100" height="100">
					<image width="0" height="0" size_to_parent="false" isee:transparency="0" isee:fixed_aspect_ratio="true"/>
				</graphics_frame>
				<button border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent="true" isee:highlight_on_hover="false" label="" isee:tooltip="How well the model represents the real-world system. It focuses on whether the essential variables, relationships, and feedback loops are included and whether the equations and assumptions accurately reflect how the system operates." x="42.9783" y="202.391" width="162.739" height="30">
					<actions>
						<action>unknown</action>
					</actions>
				</button>
				<button border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent="true" label="" isee:tooltip="Evaluates whether the model produces realistic patterns over time. This includes checking if the model can reproduce historical trends and whether its simulated future scenarios are plausible and consistent with available evidence." x="41.913" y="291.087" width="171.826" height="30">
					<actions>
						<action>unknown</action>
					</actions>
				</button>
				<button border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent="true" label="" isee:tooltip="Examines whether the model captures the underlying conceptual problem it is intended to address. It considers whether the model meaningfully represents the key mechanisms driving the issue and whether it can provide useful insights into potential solutions." x="37.7609" y="380.652" width="173.174" height="30">
					<actions>
						<action>unknown</action>
					</actions>
				</button>
				<button border_width="thin" border_style="none" transparent="true" label="" isee:tooltip="Assesses the quality and appropriateness of the data used to build and calibrate the model. It ensures that data sources are reliable, sufficient, and suitable for estimating parameters and supporting the model’s outputs." x="39.8447" y="469.348" width="117.913" height="30">
					<actions>
						<action>unknown</action>
					</actions>
				</button>
				<graphics_frame fill="none" x="655.429" y="-30.9231" width="408.571" height="581.75">
					<image width="612" height="612" size_to_parent="false" isee:transparency="0" isee:fixed_aspect_ratio="true">data:image/png;base64,</image>
				</graphics_frame>
			</view>
			<view isee:template_view="template:2" background="white" page_width="1066" page_height="600" zoom="115" type="interface">
				<style>
					<isee:stacked_container item_spacing="0" corner_radius="4" selected_item_color="black" selected_item_background="white" item_background="#DDDDDD" transparent_bg="false"/>
				</style>
				<text_box font_size="24pt" appearance="transparent" x="32.7425" y="11.6054" width="555.452" height="58">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:&apos;.AppleSystemUIFont&apos;; font-size:13pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:&apos;Arial&apos;; font-size:24pt; font-weight:700; color:#ffffff;&quot;&gt;Resources and Contact Information&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</text_box>
				<text_box x="40.485" y="83.5916" width="421.759" height="297.465">&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
